IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-s150-1-consent.l4 -- s 150.1, Consent no defence (the age bands for a complainant's consent, and mistake of age).
--
-- Ages are NUMBERS of years (a complainant "under the age of 16 years" is an age LESS THAN 16; "12 years of age or more but under the age of 14" is AT LEAST 12 and LESS THAN 14).
-- The offence charged is a core `Provision of the Code` (R1 of PLAN.md): section as a decimal and subsection as the Code writes it, "(2)"; "" for a whole section.
-- "an offence under section 151" is any provision of section 151; "an offence under subsection 153(1)" is that subsection only, so a caller gives the subsection "(1)".
-- What FALSE and NOTHING mean here (see NOTES.md, fork register F2 to F6):
--   * a charge outside the offences a subsection names, or a complainant outside its age band: NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only": the periods and scope ruling (c) of 2026-11-05);
--   * a "defence" subsection whose "if" or condition on the accused is unmet: JUST FALSE, "this section gives no defence on these facts" (the delegated-defence ruling (b) of 2026-11-05);
--   * a bar ("it is not a defence ... unless") whose "unless" is met: JUST FALSE (the "unless" is the text's own limit).

§ `s 150.1 Consent no defence`

DECLARE `s 150.1 charge` HAS
    `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the age of the complainant, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the age of the accused, in years` IS A NUMBER

-- The three relationships that paragraphs (2)(b), (2.1)(b) and (2.2)(b) rule out, and that subsection (3) turns on.
DECLARE `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant` HAS
    `the accused is in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused is a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused is in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts the two transitional subsections (2.2) and (2.3) turn on: what was so "on the day on which this subsection comes into force".
DECLARE `s 150.1 transitional facts` HAS
    `s 2 common-law partner: on the day on which subsection 150.1(2.2) came into force the accused was the complainant's common-law partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `on that day the accused had been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on that day the accused and the complainant had had, or were expecting to have, a child as a result of the relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately before the day on which subsection 150.1(2.3) came into force the accused was married to the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The lists of offences, one for each wording the subsections use. A list is tested by section number (R1); each name quotes the text.
§§ `s 150.1(1) the rule: it is not a defence that the complainant consented`

-- src:3002 | 150.1 (1) Subject to subsections (2) to (2.2), when an accused is charged with an offence under section 151 or 152 or subsection 153(1), 160(3) or 173(2) or is charged with an offence under section 271, 272 or 273 in respect of a complainant under the age of 16 years, it is not a defence that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge.
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(1) (src:3002)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(1) the offence is under section 151 or 152 or subsection 153(1), 160(3) or 173(2)` MEANS
       `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 151
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 152
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 153 "(1)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 160 "(3)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 173 "(2)"

@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(1) (src:3002)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(1) the offence is under section 271, 272 or 273` MEANS
       `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 271
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 272
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 273

@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(1) (src:3002)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 150.1 charge`
      relationship IS A `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant`
      transitional IS A `s 150.1 transitional facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(1) it is not a defence that the complainant consented` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `s 150.1(1) the offence is under section 151 or 152 or subsection 153(1), 160(3) or 173(2)` (charge's `the offence charged`)
               OR (   `s 150.1(1) the offence is under section 271, 272 or 273` (charge's `the offence charged`)
                  AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` LESS THAN 16))
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when an accused is charged with an offence under section 151 or 152 or subsection 153(1), 160(3) or 173(2) or is charged with an offence under section 271, 272 or 273 in respect of a complainant under the age of 16 years"
        IF    `s 150.1(2) it is a defence that the complainant consented, complainant aged 12 or 13` charge relationship EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 150.1(2.1) it is a defence that the complainant consented, complainant aged 14 or 15` charge relationship EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 150.1(2.2) it is a defence that the complainant consented, the accused being five or more years older` charge relationship transitional EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsections (2) to (2.2)"
        IF    `s 150.1(2.2) the charge is one that subsection (2.2) speaks to` charge
          AND `s 150.1(2.2) it is a defence that the complainant consented, the accused being five or more years older` charge relationship transitional EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (2.2) turns on s 2 "common-law partner", and that answer was not given
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The answer to "is it a defence that the complainant consented?" gathered from the five subsections, by hand (the legal effect has more than one route: ruling E1, option B as guidance for gathering by hand).
-- Subsection (1) is "Subject to subsections (2) to (2.2)": it is not subject to (2.3). Where (1) applies and (2.3) applies too, the text gives two answers and no rule of priority (fork F7).

§§ `s 150.1(2) to (2.3) the exceptions: it is a defence that the complainant consented`

-- src:3003 | Exception — complainant aged 12 or 13
-- src:3004 | (2) When an accused is charged with an offence under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271 in respect of a complainant who is 12 years of age or more but under the age of 14 years, it is a defence that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge if the accused
-- src:3005 | (a) is less than two years older than the complainant; and
-- src:3006 | (b) is not in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant, is not a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency and is not in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant.
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(2) (src:3003-3006)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(2) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271` MEANS
       `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 151
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 152
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 173 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 271

-- The same offences as paragraph (2)'s list: used for (2.1), (2.2) and (2.3) ("the accused referred to in subsection (2.1)").

@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(2)(b) (src:3006)
GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(2)(b) the accused is in none of the three relationships` MEANS
        NOT `the relationship`'s `the accused is in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant`
    AND NOT `the relationship`'s `the accused is a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency`
    AND NOT `the relationship`'s `the accused is in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant`


@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(2) (src:3003-3006)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 150.1 charge`
      relationship IS A `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(2) it is a defence that the complainant consented, complainant aged 12 or 13` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `s 150.1(2) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271` (charge's `the offence charged`)
               AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` AT LEAST 12
               AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` LESS THAN 14)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "When an accused is charged with an offence under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271 in respect of a complainant who is 12 years of age or more but under the age of 14 years"
        IF    (charge's `the age of the accused, in years` MINUS charge's `the age of the complainant, in years`) LESS THAN 2
          AND `s 150.1(2)(b) the accused is in none of the three relationships` relationship
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge if the accused (a) is less than two years older than the complainant; and (b) is not in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant"

-- src:3007 | Exception — complainant aged 14 or 15
-- src:3008 | (2.1) If an accused is charged with an offence under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271 in respect of a complainant who is 14 years of age or more but under the age of 16 years, it is a defence that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge if the accused
-- src:3009 | (a) is less than five years older than the complainant; and
-- src:3010 | (b) is not in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant, is not a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency and is not in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant.
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(2.1) (src:3007-3010)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(2.1) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271` MEANS
    `s 150.1(2) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271` `the offence charged`


@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(2.1) (src:3007-3010)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 150.1 charge`
      relationship IS A `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(2.1) it is a defence that the complainant consented, complainant aged 14 or 15` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `s 150.1(2.1) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271` (charge's `the offence charged`)
               AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` AT LEAST 14
               AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` LESS THAN 16)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a complainant who is 14 years of age or more but under the age of 16 years"
        IF    (charge's `the age of the accused, in years` MINUS charge's `the age of the complainant, in years`) LESS THAN 5
          AND `s 150.1(2)(b) the accused is in none of the three relationships` relationship
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge if the accused (a) is less than five years older than the complainant; and (b) is not in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant"

-- src:3011 | Exception for transitional purposes
-- src:3012 | (2.2) When the accused referred to in subsection (2.1) is five or more years older than the complainant, it is a defence that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge if, on the day on which this subsection comes into force,
-- src:3013 | (a) the accused is the common-law partner of the complainant, or has been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year and they have had or are expecting to have a child as a result of the relationship; and
-- src:3014 | (b) the accused is not in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant, is not a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency and is not in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant.
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(2.2) (src:3011-3014)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 150.1 charge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(2.2) the charge is one that subsection (2.2) speaks to` MEANS
        `s 150.1(2.1) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271` (charge's `the offence charged`)
    AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` AT LEAST 14
    AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` LESS THAN 16
    AND (charge's `the age of the accused, in years` MINUS charge's `the age of the complainant, in years`) AT LEAST 5

@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(2.2) (src:3011-3014)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 150.1 charge`
      relationship IS A `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant`
      transitional IS A `s 150.1 transitional facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(2.2) it is a defence that the complainant consented, the accused being five or more years older` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 150.1(2.2) the charge is one that subsection (2.2) speaks to` charge)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "When the accused referred to in subsection (2.1) is five or more years older than the complainant"
        IF `the partner limb (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 150.1(2)(b) the accused is in none of the three relationships` relationship
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the partner limb (a)` EQUALS NOTHING AND `s 150.1(2)(b) the accused is in none of the three relationships` relationship
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the accused is the common-law partner of the complainant"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge if, on the day on which this subsection comes into force, (a) the accused is the common-law partner of the complainant, or has been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year and they have had or are expecting to have a child as a result of the relationship; and (b) the accused is not in a position of trust or authority"
    WHERE
        -- (a): common-law partner, or cohabiting for less than a year and a child had or expected.
        `the partner limb (a)` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF transitional's `s 2 common-law partner: on the day on which subsection 150.1(2.2) came into force the accused was the complainant's common-law partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                IF    transitional's `on that day the accused had been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year`
                  AND transitional's `on that day the accused and the complainant had had, or were expecting to have, a child as a result of the relationship` THEN JUST TRUE
                IF transitional's `s 2 common-law partner: on the day on which subsection 150.1(2.2) came into force the accused was the complainant's common-law partner` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the accused is the common-law partner of the complainant, or has been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year and they have had or are expecting to have a child"
                OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the accused is the common-law partner of the complainant"

-- src:3015 | Exception for transitional purposes
-- src:3016 | (2.3) If, immediately before the day on which this subsection comes into force, the accused referred to in subsection (2.1) is married to the complainant, it is a defence that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge.
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(2.3) (src:3015-3016)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 150.1 charge`
      transitional IS A `s 150.1 transitional facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(2.3) it is a defence that the complainant consented, the accused being married to the complainant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `s 150.1(2.1) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 173(2) or section 271` (charge's `the offence charged`)
               AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` AT LEAST 14
               AND charge's `the age of the complainant, in years` LESS THAN 16)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the accused referred to in subsection (2.1)"
        IF transitional's `immediately before the day on which subsection 150.1(2.3) came into force the accused was married to the complainant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, immediately before the day on which this subsection comes into force, the accused referred to in subsection (2.1) is married to the complainant, it is a defence"


-- (the gathering function below cites subsections (1) to (2.3) without a locator: it is not a provision of the text)
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(1), (2), (2.1), (2.2) and (2.3), gathered by hand
DECLARE `s 150.1 consent as a defence` IS ONE OF
    `s 150.1 consent is not a defence, by subsection (1)`
    `s 150.1 consent is a defence, by subsection (2), (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3)`
    `s 150.1 subsection (1) says consent is not a defence and subsection (2.3) says it is, and the text does not say which prevails`
    `s 150.1 section 150.1 does not say whether consent is a defence`

GIVEN charge IS A `s 150.1 charge`
      relationship IS A `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant`
      transitional IS A `s 150.1 transitional facts`
GIVETH A `s 150.1 consent as a defence`
`s 150.1 whether it is a defence that the complainant consented` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    `s 150.1(1) it is not a defence that the complainant consented` charge relationship transitional EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `s 150.1(2.3) it is a defence that the complainant consented, the accused being married to the complainant` charge transitional EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `s 150.1 subsection (1) says consent is not a defence and subsection (2.3) says it is, and the text does not say which prevails`
        IF    `s 150.1(2) it is a defence that the complainant consented, complainant aged 12 or 13` charge relationship EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 150.1(2.1) it is a defence that the complainant consented, complainant aged 14 or 15` charge relationship EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 150.1(2.2) it is a defence that the complainant consented, the accused being five or more years older` charge relationship transitional EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 150.1(2.3) it is a defence that the complainant consented, the accused being married to the complainant` charge transitional EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `s 150.1 consent is a defence, by subsection (2), (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3)`
        IF `s 150.1(1) it is not a defence that the complainant consented` charge relationship transitional EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `s 150.1 consent is not a defence, by subsection (1)`
        OTHERWISE `s 150.1 section 150.1 does not say whether consent is a defence`

§§ `s 150.1(3) a person aged twelve or thirteen`

-- src:3017 | Exemption for accused aged twelve or thirteen
-- src:3018 | (3) No person aged twelve or thirteen years shall be tried for an offence under section 151 or 152 or subsection 173(2) unless the person is in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant, is a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency or is in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant.
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(3) (src:3017-3018)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(3) the offence is under section 151 or 152 or subsection 173(2)` MEANS
       `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 151
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 152
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 173 "(2)"

@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(3) (src:3017-3018)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the age of the accused, in years` IS A NUMBER
      relationship IS A `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(3) no person aged twelve or thirteen shall be tried: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `s 150.1(3) the offence is under section 151 or 152 or subsection 173(2)` `the offence charged`
               AND `the age of the accused, in years` AT LEAST 12
               AND `the age of the accused, in years` LESS THAN 14)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person aged twelve or thirteen years shall be tried for an offence under section 151 or 152 or subsection 173(2)"
        IF    relationship's `the accused is in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant`
           OR relationship's `the accused is a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency`
           OR relationship's `the accused is in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person is in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant, is a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency or is in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 150.1(4) to (6) mistake of age`

-- src:3019 | Mistake of age
-- src:3020 | (4) It is not a defence to a charge under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2), or section 271, 272 or 273 that the accused believed that the complainant was 16 years of age or more at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed unless the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant.
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(4) (src:3019-3020)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(4) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2), or section 271, 272 or 273` MEANS
       `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 151
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 152
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 160 "(3)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 173 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 271
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 272
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 273

@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(4) (src:3019-3020)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the accused believed that the complainant was 16 years of age or more at the time of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(4) the belief that the complainant was 16 or more is not a defence: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `s 150.1(4) the offence is under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2), or section 271, 272 or 273` `the offence charged`
               AND `the accused believed that the complainant was 16 years of age or more at the time of the offence`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a charge under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2), or section 271, 272 or 273 that the accused believed that the complainant was 16 years of age or more"
        IF `the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

