    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 171
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 172
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 279.011
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 279.02 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 279.03 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 286.1 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 286.2 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence charged` 286.3 "(2)"

@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(5) (src:3021-3022)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the accused believed that the complainant was 18 years of age or more at the time of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(5) the belief that the complainant was 18 or more is not a defence: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `s 150.1(5) the offence is under section 153, 170, 171, 172 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2)` `the offence charged`
               AND `the accused believed that the complainant was 18 years of age or more at the time of the offence`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a charge under section 153, 170, 171, 172 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2) that the accused believed that the complainant was 18 years of age or more"
        IF `the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3023 | Mistake of age
-- src:3024 | (6) An accused cannot raise a mistaken belief in the age of the complainant in order to invoke a defence under subsection (2) or (2.1) unless the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant.
@ref Criminal Code s 150.1(6) (src:3023-3024)
GIVEN `the accused raises a mistaken belief in the age of the complainant in order to invoke a defence under subsection (2) or (2.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150.1(6) the accused cannot raise a mistaken belief in the age of the complainant to invoke subsection (2) or (2.1): the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused raises a mistaken belief in the age of the complainant in order to invoke a defence under subsection (2) or (2.1)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused cannot raise a mistaken belief in the age of the complainant in order to invoke a defence under subsection (2) or (2.1)"
        IF `the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
